`fetchTasks` can be invoked multiple times in quick succession (page changes, search debounce, filter changes). Without cancellation / staleness protection, a slower response for an earlier page/query can overwrite state after a later request completes. Consider using an `AbortController` per request or a monotonically increasing request id check before calling `setTasks`/`setTotalCount`.

