> +  const toDateString = (ts?: string) =>
+    ts ? new Date(ts).toISOString().split('T')[0] : '';

`toDateString` uses `new Date(ts).toISOString().split('T')[0]`, which converts to UTC before truncating. For users outside UTC this can shift the resulting date by ±1 day. Prefer formatting from local date parts (e.g. via `toYYYYMMDD(new Date(ts))`) or keep the original ISO string and format for display when rendering.


> +  const doFetch = (accessToken: string) =>
+    fetch(url, {
+      ...options,
+      headers: {
+        ...options.headers,
+        'User-Token': accessToken,
+      },
+    });

Merging headers via `{ ...options.headers, 'User-Token': accessToken }` will silently drop headers when `options.headers` is a `Headers` instance (spreading it produces `{}`). Consider normalizing with `new Headers(options.headers)` and then setting `User-Token`, so this helper works reliably for all `RequestInit.headers` shapes.


> +              {layouts.map(({ id, col, totalCols }) => {
+                const event = dayEvents.find((e) => e.id === id)!;
+                const { top, height } = getEventPosition(event);
+                const pct = 100 / totalCols;

`layouts.map(...)` does a `dayEvents.find(...)` for each layout entry, making this O(n²) per day column. For larger event lists this can add noticeable render cost. Consider building an `id -> event` map once per column/day (or changing `layoutEvents` to return indices) and doing O(1) lookups in the render loop.

> +            {layouts.map(({ id, col, totalCols }) => {
+              const event = todayEvents.find((e) => e.id === id)!;
               const { top, height } = getEventPosition(event);
+              const pct = 100 / totalCols;

`layouts.map(...)` does a `todayEvents.find(...)` for each layout entry, making this O(n²) for the day. Consider building an `id -> event` map once, or have `layoutEvents` return indices, so the render loop stays O(n).

> +import { useState, useEffect, useCallback } from 'react';
