The PR title/description focuses on a DayView card layout tweak, but this change set also introduces a new Tasker API client, replaces mock data with live fetching in Tasks/Schedule screens, and adds complete/postpone/delete actions. Please update the PR description/title to reflect the broader scope, or split the API integration into a separate PR to keep review risk manageable.

> +  // Use local date so early-morning events in UTC- zones land on the correct day
+  const date = toYYYYMMDD(new Date(task.startTime));
+  return {
+    id: task.id,
+    title: task.title,
+    startTime: startHHMM,
+    endTime: endHHMM,
+    date,

`event.date` is being stored as a `YYYY-MM-DD` string derived from `new Date(task.startTime)`. Other parts of the UI (e.g. ScheduleSummary) still parse `event.date` via `new Date(event.date)` which treats `YYYY-MM-DD` as UTC and can shift the day in non-UTC timezones. Consider either storing a full ISO timestamp for the date field, or updating all consumers to compare using `toYYYYMMDD(...)` rather than `new Date(...)` parsing.

>    const [filterCategory, setFilterCategory] = useState<string>('all');
   const [searchQuery, setSearchQuery] = useState('');

`filterCategory` now represents both status and category filter ids (e.g. 'planned', 'work'), not just categories. Renaming this state (and related props) to something like `currentFilter` would make the intent clearer and reduce confusion during future changes.

> @@ -52,7 +48,9 @@ const TaskList = ({ tasks, onTaskSelect, selectedTaskId }: TaskListProps) => {
   };
 
   const formatDate = (dateString: string) => {
+    if (!dateString) return null;
     const date = new Date(dateString);

Parsing `YYYY-MM-DD` with `new Date(dateString)` treats it as UTC per spec, which can shift the displayed day in non-UTC timezones and break the Today/Tomorrow comparisons. If `deadline` is a date-only value, consider parsing it as local (e.g. append `T00:00:00` without `Z`) or carry an ISO timestamp and format for display using local getters.


> +      let from: Date;
+      let till: Date;
+      if (viewMode === 'week') {
+        from = new Date(currentDate);
+        // (getDay() + 6) % 7 maps Sun=0→6, Mon=1→0, ..., Sat=6→5, giving days since Monday
+        from.setDate(currentDate.getDate() - ((currentDate.getDay() + 6) % 7));
+        till = new Date(from);
+        till.setDate(from.getDate() + 6);
+      } else {
+        from = new Date(currentDate);
+        till = new Date(currentDate);
+      }
+      const response = await listTasks({
+        from: toApiDateParam(from),
+        till: toApiDateParam(till),
+        pageSize: 100,

`pageSize` is set to 100 here, but the backend `ListTasksV1Request.page_size` is validated with `lte: 20` (see task.proto). This request will consistently fail with InvalidArgument; either keep pageSize <= 20 and paginate, or make multiple requests to fetch all pages for the selected date range.


